            "`--dns-transport <list>` chooses the transports, `udp`, `tcp`, `tls` and `quic` (default `udp,tcp`), each once. `tls` is DNS over TLS (DoT, RFC 7858): TLS from the first byte, then the same two-byte-length messages as TCP, and it needs `--cert` or `--self-signed` (else exit 58). The handshake agrees ALPN `dot`, accepts a client that offers none and ends one that offers only other protocols with alert `no_application_protocol`. A listen URL with a port puts every transport on it; one without puts each on its default, 53 for `udp` and `tcp` and 853 for `tls` and `quic`. `tcp` with `tls` on one explicit port is refused, exit 2: `surl: --dns-transport tcp and tls cannot share port <n>`. `quic` is DNS over QUIC (DoQ, RFC 9250) on UDP: TLS 1.3 only, ALPN `doq`, it needs `--cert` or `--self-signed` (else exit 58), and it is refused, exit 2, with `udp` on one explicit port (`surl: --dns-transport udp and quic cannot share port <n>`) and on port 53 (`surl: --dns-transport quic cannot use port 53`).",
