        ["imap"] =
        [
            "The IMAP server (IMAP4rev1, RFC 3501) serves the mail store the SMTP server delivers into, so mail sent over `smtp://` is read over `imap://` in the same run. `curl -u user:password imap://127.0.0.1:<port>/` lists the mailboxes, `curl -u user:password 'imap://127.0.0.1:<port>/INBOX;UID=1'` fetches one message, `curl -T <file> imap://127.0.0.1:<port>/INBOX` appends one, and `curl -X '<command>'` sends any other command, such as `SEARCH`, `STORE` or `EXPUNGE`.",
            "Every command that reads or changes a mailbox needs a login unless `--allow-anonymous` is given, when it opens one anonymous set of mailboxes. `curl -u user:password` logs in with `LOGIN`, or with `AUTHENTICATE` and a SASL mechanism `--auth` accepts (`curl --login-options AUTH=<mech>`, see the auth topic); over `imap://` without STARTTLS, `LOGIN`, PLAIN and LOGIN are not offered unless `--allow-plaintext-auth` is given, and CRAM-MD5 is.",
            "With `--cert` or `--self-signed`, `imap://` offers STARTTLS (`curl --ssl-reqd`); without a certificate STARTTLS is answered `BAD STARTTLS not available`. `imaps` is the same server over TLS from the first byte, so an `imaps` listen URL needs `--cert` or `--self-signed` (see the tls topic).",
            "Without `--directory` the mail store lives in memory only; with it, it is kept in `<path>/.surl/mail` and loaded at start, and an index or message file that cannot be read or does not parse exits 37. An `APPEND` past `--max-filesize` is answered `NO [TOOBIG]` and not stored; a command, its literals included, longer than `--max-line` is answered `BAD Command line too long`, and one not finished within `--head-timeout` `* BYE`.",
